    options: ["Small fish build up in number around a FAD, where algae grow and there is shelter.", "Drifting FADs can carry tuna and other predators outside their normal range.", "Fish gathered at a FAD may change their natural behaviour, such as their feeding and migration routes.", "FADs that are lost or break loose keep drifting and go on entangling turtles and sharks.", "Turtles and sharks tend to keep away from FADs, so these animals are rarely put at risk.", "FADs are towed along the seabed by the boats fishing around them, damaging habitats.", "A FAD supplies so much food that the tuna population grows faster than boats can fish it."],
